 # Changelog
 
+## S306p A PUSH TO MAIN STARTS A ROUND (the framework's thin path; P-885; main's M86 point 1) (2026-11-28)
+
+- **`.github/workflows/intake.yml`:** the trigger `push: branches: [main]`, beside the hourly cron and the manual trigger.
+  Only main pushes to main (setting 3), so the code a push runs is main's own; a seat's push to its own branch starts
+  nothing. No pull-request trigger. The concurrency group keeps one round at a time.
+- **The test of the triggers** (`tests/test_queue_intake.py`) holds `push` limited to `main` and refuses `pull_request`
+  and `pull_request_target`; the queue's README, setting 5, says so.
+
